infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title "No codegen" vs codegen: what the trade actually buys
  desc tRPC shares a TS type for live inference; OpenAPI/GraphQL generate a language-agnostic wire contract
  compares
    - label tRPC (no codegen)
      children
        - label Zero generated files
          desc Client type = typeof appRouter, recomputed by tsc
        - label Live inference per keystroke
          desc Rename a server procedure and the client breaks instantly
        - label Needs a shared TS type
          desc Same build / monorepo; TypeScript on both ends
        - label No polyglot clients
          desc A type crosses a compile boundary, not network or language
        - label Cost: inference time
          desc Big router → tsc and editor crawl; no file to cache
    - label OpenAPI / GraphQL (codegen)
      children
        - label Generates a client file
          desc From an OpenAPI spec or a GraphQL schema
        - label Read once, not re-inferred
          desc Generated file wins on compiler performance
        - label Language-agnostic contract
          desc A real wire format, not a TypeScript type
        - label Polyglot + third-party
          desc Swift, Kotlin, separately-built service clients work
        - label Cost: a build step
          desc Must regenerate whenever the API changes
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f59e0b
